{
  "name": "LLM as a Judge (4 + judge)",
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": true
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "manual-trigger",
      "name": "When clicking ‘Execute workflow’",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "value": "You are an expert in clinical terminology and medical knowledge representation.\n\nDesign a formula that measures how useful a candidate concept would be in an existing target ontology. The score will determine whether or not to insert the concept into the ontology. Identify and explain the factors the formula should consider.\n\nI am building a framework that decides whether a new concept should be added to an existing ontology. A high-utility concept should be inserted, whereas a low-utility concept should not.\n\nTreat utility as a function of the current content of the target ontology only, such as MeSH, SNOMED CT, MedDRA, ICD10-CM, NCIt, OMIM, BERO and GO.\n\nProvide a justification for every factor in the formula. For each factor, explain: What does it measure? Why is it important? How does it influence the final score? Any assumptions?\n\nReturn your answer as: (1) the proposed formula in plain text, (2) a list of factors, (3) assumptions or limitations.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "models",
              "name": "models",
              "value": "={{ [\"openai/gpt-5.6-sol\", \"moonshotai/kimi-k3\", \"qwen/qwen3.7-max\", \"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"] }}",
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "id": "model_configs",
              "name": "model_configs",
              "value": "={{({\n  \"anthropic/claude-opus-4.8\": {\n    \"thinking\": {\"type\": \"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\": 32000},\n    \"output_config\": {\"effort\": \"high\"},\n    \"max_tokens\": 65536\n  },\n  \"openai/gpt-5.6-sol\": {\n    \"reasoning\": {\"effort\": \"high\"},\n    \"max_tokens\": 65536\n  },\n  \"moonshotai/kimi-k3\": {\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"high\",\n    \"max_tokens\": 32768,\n    \"omit_temperature\": true\n  },\n  \"qwen/qwen3.7-max\": {\n    \"enable_thinking\": true,\n    \"thinking_budget\": 32768,\n    \"max_tokens\": 65536\n  },\n  \"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview\": {\n    \"thinking_level\": \"high\",\n    \"max_tokens\": 65536\n  }\n})}}",
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "id": "judge",
              "name": "judge_model",
              "value": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "set-config",
      "name": "Config (4 authors + judge)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [240, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/runs",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"prompt\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.prompt) }},\n  \"models\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.models) }},\n  \"judge_model\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.judge_model) }},\n  \"model_configs\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.model_configs) }}\n}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        }
      },
      "id": "create-run",
      "name": "1. Create run",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [480, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/runs/{{ $json.run_id }}/primary",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 900000
        }
      },
      "id": "phase-primary",
      "name": "2. Primary (4 LLMs)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [720, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/runs/{{ $json.run_id }}/critiques",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 900000
        }
      },
      "id": "phase-critiques",
      "name": "3. Critiques (12 calls)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [960, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/runs/{{ $json.run_id }}/refine",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 900000
        }
      },
      "id": "phase-refine",
      "name": "4. Refine (12 calls)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1200, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/runs/{{ $json.run_id }}/judge",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 900000
        }
      },
      "id": "phase-judge",
      "name": "5. Judge (pick best)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1440, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const data = $input.first().json;\nconst authors = data.authors || [];\nconst judgmentBlocks = authors.map(a => {\n  return `### LLM ${a.author_index} — ${a.model}\\n\\n${a.judgment || '_empty_'}`;\n}).join('\\n\\n');\n\nconst markdown = [\n  `# LLM-as-judge ${data.run_id}`,\n  `Judge: \\`${data.judge_model}\\` | API calls: ${data.api_calls}`,\n  '',\n  '## Judge selections',\n  judgmentBlocks,\n  '',\n  `Saved under: ${data.output_dir || ''}`,\n].join('\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    run_id: data.run_id,\n    phase: data.phase,\n    judge_model: data.judge_model,\n    api_calls: data.api_calls,\n    judgments: authors.map(a => ({\n      model: a.model,\n      judgment: a.judgment,\n    })),\n    markdown,\n    output_dir: data.output_dir,\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "format-summary",
      "name": "Format summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1680, 300]
    }
  ],
